public class Ratings {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int total = 5, count = 2;
        double wrong = total / count;             // 2.0: int division first.
        double right = (double) total / count;    // 2.5: double division.

        long bytes = 3_000_000_000L;
        int bad = (int) bytes;                    // -1294967296: silent narrowing.
        // int safe = Math.toIntExact(bytes);     // throws ArithmeticException instead.

        String name = null;
        boolean hasA = name != null && name.startsWith("A");   // short-circuit: no NPE.

        int x = 3;
        int y = x++ + x;                          // left to right: 3 + 4 = 7, x is 4.
        System.out.println(wrong + " " + right + " " + bad + " " + hasA + " " + y);
    }
}
```

| Expression | Type | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `5 / 2`. | int. | 2. |
| `5.0 / 2`. | double. | 2.5. |
| `5 % 2`. | int. | 1. |
| `(int) 3.9`. | int. | 3 (truncates). |
| `1_000_000 * 3000`. | int. | overflows! |

